; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR MORSE RECEIVER v11  -  key it on the Input switch   (loads at $4000, VM1)
;                                 the text can go into a LITE-WRITER 2 slot
; ==========================================================================
; Load, cold-boot. It asks for a Lite-Writer 2 slot (1-4; that slot's old text is
; replaced; Enter = do not save), then roughly how fast you key (5-25 WPM, Enter = 12).
; Key Morse on the Elf2K's Input switch (EF4). Each letter appears on the terminal
; (and the hex display) as you finish it, and goes into the slot at once; a longer
; pause is a word space. Q follows the key. Q or ESC on the terminal quits.
;
; TO EDIT IT: load Lite-Writer-2.lst (a build that keeps the slots - 2026-10-03 or
; later), run it, press ^L and the slot number.
;
; IT LEARNS YOUR HAND: running averages of your dots and dashes decide dot or dash,
; and separate averages of YOUR gaps - inside a letter, between letters, between
; words - decide where letters and words end. The first six marks are learned at
; double speed. The learning runs as native 1802 code ($4300, via $F1 RUNMC); the
; slot writer is native too ($4D00 open the slot, $4DE0 append a character).
;
; Limits found in testing: if you key much FASTER than you told it (a third faster)
; the first letter or two may come out wrong while it learns; a very uneven hand at
; 18+ WPM can split a letter now and then. Best at 5-20 WPM.
;
; NEEDS the GETEFA mask patch (in V0061.34 and later): the key is bit 3 of GETEFA's mask.
; Uses VM4's block for the slot pool ($7001-$7EFF) as Lite-Writer 2 does; $7000 stays $00.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/morse_rx11_verify.py): ALL PASS 2026-10-03, timed in machine cycles: 12/20/8/15 WPM, jitter, a sloppy hand, told 12 keyed 15, punctuation, a long message, a rerun, the first key 0.8-4 s after Listening; slot 2 replaced with 1 and 3 kept byte for byte; Enter = nothing saved; garbage pool x6; a full pool. KNOWN LIMIT (v10 the same): a hand slowing 18 -> 8 WPM within a few letters splits letters.
; NOT YET RUN ON HARDWARE.
;
; 251 STELLAR commands (+ the native learning step and slot writer).
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START
; D 4001 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A
; D 4005 11 0B 00 00    LOADXI R11 0000
; D 4009 0A 00          SETQ 00
; D 400B 11 0E 07 80    LOADXI R14 0780
; D 400F C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; ASKS:
; D 4011 11 0E 08 E8    LOADXI R14 08E8
; D 4015 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 4017 11 0C 0A 00    LOADXI R12 0A00
; D 401B 11 0D 0A 00    LOADXI R13 0A00
; D 401F C2 CD          GETSTR R12 R13                     the answer
; D 4021 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; D 4025 2E 04 0A 00    READIDX R4 0A00                    its first character
; D 4029 21 0A          COPYAX Acc -> R10
; D 402B 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10
; D 402D A0 00 70       IFTRUEI S0                         Enter alone: do not save
; D 4030 11 04 00 01    LOADXI R4 0001
; D 4034 2E 04 0A 00    READIDX R4 0A00
; D 4038 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 403B A1 00 11       IFFALSEI ASKS                      one character only
; D 403E 11 09 00 31    LOADXI R9 0031
; D 4042 89 A9          TESTLXY R10 < R9
; D 4044 A0 00 11       IFTRUEI ASKS
; D 4047 11 09 00 35    LOADXI R9 0035
; D 404B 88 A9          TESTGXY R10 >= R9
; D 404D A0 00 11       IFTRUEI ASKS                       not 1-4: ask again
; D 4050 53 0A 00 30    SUBXI R10 0030
; D 4054 22 0A          COPYXA R10 -> Acc
; D 4056 2F 0B 0B 10    WRITEIDX R11 0B10                  the slot
; D 405A F1 4D 00       RUNMC 4D00                         drop the slot's old text, start it afresh at the end of the pool
; D 405D 2E 0B 0B 16    READIDX R11 0B16
; D 4061 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 4064 A0 00 7B       IFTRUEI ASK
; D 4067 11 0E 09 32    LOADXI R14 0932
; D 406B C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 406D B0 00 7B       GAL ASK
; S0:
; D 4070 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 4073 2F 0B 0B 10    WRITEIDX R11 0B10                  slot 0: not saving
; D 4077 2F 0B 0B 16    WRITEIDX R11 0B16
; ASK:
; D 407B 11 0E 08 8A    LOADXI R14 088A
; D 407F C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 4081 11 0C 0A 00    LOADXI R12 0A00
; D 4085 11 0D 0A 00    LOADXI R13 0A00
; D 4089 C2 CD          GETSTR R12 R13                     the number
; D 408B 11 07 00 00    LOADXI R7 0000
; D 408F 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; DIG:
; D 4093 2E 04 0A 00    READIDX R4 0A00                    next character
; D 4097 21 0A          COPYAX Acc -> R10
; D 4099 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10
; D 409B A0 00 C0       IFTRUEI DGD
; D 409E 11 09 00 30    LOADXI R9 0030
; D 40A2 89 A9          TESTLXY R10 < R9
; D 40A4 A0 00 7B       IFTRUEI ASK                        not a digit: ask again
; D 40A7 11 09 00 3A    LOADXI R9 003A
; D 40AB 88 A9          TESTGXY R10 >= R9
; D 40AD A0 00 7B       IFTRUEI ASK
; D 40B0 53 0A 00 30    SUBXI R10 0030
; D 40B4 4A 7F          MULTXY R7 * R15
; D 40B6 21 17          COPYAX MA -> R7                    W x 10
; D 40B8 50 7A 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R10 -> R7              + the digit
; D 40BB 42 04          INCX R4
; D 40BD B0 00 93       GAL DIG
; DGD:
; D 40C0 8C 07          TESTXZ R7
; D 40C2 A1 00 C9       IFFALSEI HAVE
; D 40C5 11 07 00 0C    LOADXI R7 000C                     Enter alone: 12
; HAVE:
; D 40C9 11 09 00 05    LOADXI R9 0005
; D 40CD 89 79          TESTLXY R7 < R9
; D 40CF A0 00 7B       IFTRUEI ASK
; D 40D2 11 09 00 1A    LOADXI R9 001A
; D 40D6 88 79          TESTGXY R7 >= R9
; D 40D8 A0 00 7B       IFTRUEI ASK
; D 40DB 11 0E 08 CC    LOADXI R14 08CC
; D 40DF C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       printed FIRST: PRINTSTR uses RE, which then holds a gap average
; D 40E1 11 01 00 73    LOADXI R1 0073
; D 40E5 23 00 7A       COPYXY R7 -> R10
; D 40E8 11 09 00 02    LOADXI R9 0002
; D 40EC 4D A9          DIVXY R10 / R9
; D 40EE 25             COPYMAA
; D 40EF 21 09          COPYAX Acc -> R9
; D 40F1 50 19 01       ADDXYZ R1 + R9 -> R1
; D 40F4 4D 17          DIVXY R1 / R7
; D 40F6 25             COPYMAA
; D 40F7 21 01          COPYAX Acc -> R1                   dot = 106 / WPM samples, rounded
; D 40F9 50 11 02       ADDXYZ R1 + R1 -> R2
; D 40FC 50 21 02       ADDXYZ R2 + R1 -> R2               dash = 3 dots
; D 40FF 50 11 0E       ADDXYZ R1 + R1 -> R14              gap in a letter: 1 dot (x2: the gap loop counts in twos)
; D 4102 50 EE 0F       ADDXYZ R14 + R14 -> R15
; D 4105 50 FE 0F       ADDXYZ R15 + R14 -> R15            3 dots (x2) ...
; D 4108 23 00 17       COPYXY R1 -> R7
; D 410B 61 72          SHIFTBX R7 right 1
; D 410D 50 F7 0F       ADDXYZ R15 + R7 -> R15             ... + a quarter dot: between letters 3.25 to start
; D 4110 50 EE 07       ADDXYZ R14 + R14 -> R7
; D 4113 50 77 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R7 -> R7
; D 4116 50 77 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R7 -> R7
; D 4119 51 7E 07       SUBXYZ R7 - R14 -> R7              between words: 7 dots (x2: 16 - 2 = 14)
; D 411C 11 0A 0B 00    LOADXI R10 0B00
; D 4120 3A 02 7A       COPYXMY R7 -> M(R10)
; D 4123 11 07 00 00    LOADXI R7 0000
; D 4127 52 0A 00 02    ADDXI R10 0002
; D 412B 3A 02 7A       COPYXMY R7 -> M(R10)               no marks seen yet: learn fast for the first six
; D 412E 50 12 03       ADDXYZ R1 + R2 -> R3               dot + dash
; D 4131 50 EF 0C       ADDXYZ R14 + R15 -> R12
; D 4134 61 C2          SHIFTBX R12 right 1                LETTER = midway: inside a letter / between letters
; D 4136 11 0A 0B 00    LOADXI R10 0B00
; D 413A 39 02 A9       COPYMXY M(R10) -> R9
; D 413D 50 9F 09       ADDXYZ R9 + R15 -> R9
; D 4140 61 92          SHIFTBX R9 right 1                 WORD = midway: between letters / words
; D 4142 50 11 07       ADDXYZ R1 + R1 -> R7
; D 4145 50 77 0A       ADDXYZ R7 + R7 -> R10              RA = 4 dots (x2)
; D 4148 23 00 17       COPYXY R1 -> R7
; D 414B 61 72          SHIFTBX R7 right 1
; D 414D 50 71 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R1 -> R7
; D 4150 50 7A 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R10 -> R7              5.5 (x2) = 2.75 dots
; D 4153 89 7C          TESTLXY R7 < R12
; D 4155 A1 01 5B       IFFALSEI CL1s
; D 4158 23 00 7C       COPYXY R7 -> R12
; CL1s:
; D 415B 50 AA 07       ADDXYZ R10 + R10 -> R7
; D 415E 50 71 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R1 -> R7               9 (x2) = 4.5 dots
; D 4161 89 97          TESTLXY R9 < R7
; D 4163 A1 01 69       IFFALSEI CL2s
; D 4166 23 00 79       COPYXY R7 -> R9
; CL2s:
; D 4169 50 7A 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R10 -> R7              13 (x2) = 6.5 dots
; D 416C 89 79          TESTLXY R7 < R9
; D 416E A1 01 74       IFFALSEI CL3s
; D 4171 23 00 79       COPYXY R7 -> R9
; CL3s:
; D 4174 11 05 00 01    LOADXI R5 0001                     no elements yet
; D 4178 11 06 00 00    LOADXI R6 0000
; D 417C 11 08 00 00    LOADXI R8 0000
; UP:
; D 4180 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; UL:
; D 4184 CC             SERST                              a key on the terminal?
; D 4185 A0 01 F5       IFTRUEI TKEY
; D 4188 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 418B 09             GETEFA                             EF1-4 as a mask
; D 418C 1A 08          TESTBITI 08                        EF4: the Input switch
; D 418E A0 01 C8       IFTRUEI DOWN                       the key went down
; D 4191 52 04 00 02    ADDXI R4 0002                      the gap loop counts in TWOS: R4 = 2 x gap, no doubling needed
; D 4195 88 4C          TESTGXY R4 >= R12
; D 4197 A0 01 A8       IFTRUEI PAST                       past LETTER: the decisions
; D 419A C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 419B C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 419C C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 419D C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 419E C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 419F C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 41A0 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 41A1 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 41A2 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 41A3 C0 01          DLYI 01                            one sample
; D 41A5 B0 01 84       GAL UL
; PAST:
; D 41A8 86 05 00 01    TESTXI R5 0001
; D 41AC A0 01 B2       IFTRUEI P1                         nothing keyed, or done already
; D 41AF BD 02 4A       CALL LETTER                        the letter is complete
; P1:
; D 41B2 88 49          TESTGXY R4 >= R9
; D 41B4 A1 01 C4       IFFALSEI P1X                       past WORD:
; D 41B7 8C 06          TESTXZ R6
; D 41B9 A0 01 BF       IFTRUEI P2
; D 41BC BD 02 75       CALL SPACE                           a word gap
; P2:
; D 41BF C0 01          DLYI 01                            one sample
; D 41C1 B0 01 84       GAL UL
; P1X:
; D 41C4 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 41C5 B0 01 BF       GAL P2                             padded: every sample of a gap is the same length
; DOWN:
; D 41C8 0A 01          SETQ 01                            Q follows the key
; D 41CA 23 00 4D       COPYXY R4 -> R13                   RD = the gap that just ended - learned from after this mark
; D 41CD 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; DL:
; D 41D1 42 04          INCX R4
; D 41D3 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
; D 41D4 C4             NOP                                pad: evens the two sampling loops
